                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_309">Letheringham
                            (Crew), Suffolk, Augustinian priory of St Mary the Virgin</orgName>
                            <p>This attribution was accepted (albeit with a query) in the second
                            edition of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964). However, the
                            attribution was later rejected in the Supplement (1987). The
                            corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card shows that
                            the source of the attribution was De Ricci, <title>Census</title>, 1,
                            1027. <q>Written for Lord Hastings, beheaded in 1483 ...; belonged to
                            Letheringham Abbey (Suffolk)</q>. However, Ker later added the following
                            note on the card: but the only evidence for Letheringham ownership is
                            <q>Abbatiae de Letheringham Suffolkiae</q> written in a late 17th
                            century hand on fol. 1.</p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName role="fmo">I. (or T.) Leman,
                            c. 1810. No. 2667 in an early 19th century
                            catalogue.</persName></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName role="fmo">George
                            Dunn</persName>, bought March 1898, sold 1913 (no. 239).</provenance>
                    </history>
